        "2": {
          "evidence": "Five distinct orange data points are visible in the plot area, each accompanied by a text label: 'Center A', 'Center B', 'Center C', 'Center D', and 'Center E'.",
          "status": "supported"
        }
      },
      "B": {
        "reading_checked": "If the chart is explicitly limited to selected high-referral centers, then its pattern may be affected by selection and does not by itself characterize all centers in the network; such evidence can be retained as contextual information pending broader comparison. Applies if no additional network-wide sampling, comparison group, or outcome evidence is supplied.",
        "evidence": "The subtitle explicitly states the data is for 'Selected high-referral centers', confirming the chart is a subset rather than the entire network. The condition that 'no additional network-wide sampling... is supplied' is met because the provided context contains only this specific dashboard and no other datasets. The inference that a selected subset does not characterize the whole network is a standard statistical principle supported by the visible limitation in the subtitle.",
        "status": "supported"
      }
    },
    "r2": {
      "O": {
        "1": {
          "evidence": "The title 'Top Screening Centers: Outreach Hours vs Referral Count' and subtitle 'Selected high-referral centers shown in dashboard summary.' are clearly visible at the top of the chart.",
          "status": "supported"
        },
        "2": {
          "evidence": "The x-axis is labeled 'Monthly outreach hours' with visible tick marks at 30, 40, 50, 60, and 70. The y-axis is labeled 'Referral count' with visible tick marks at 60, 80, 100, 120, 140, and 160.",
          "status": "supported"
        },
        "3": {
          "evidence": "Visually, Center A is at the bottom-left (approx x=32, y=61). Center B is to the right and higher (approx x=42, y=74). Center C is further right and higher (approx x=52, y=90). Center D is further right and higher (approx x=62, y=117). Center E is at the top-right (approx x=72, y=163). The points form a clear monotonic increasing sequence from left to right.",
          "status": "supported"
        }
      },
      "B": {
        "reading_checked": "If the horizontal axis encodes monthly outreach hours increasing left-to-right and the vertical axis encodes referral count increasing upward, then the labeled center points can be compared as an observed association. A consistent higher-hours/higher-referrals pattern among the displayed selected centers is suitable for broader network review, but this cross-sectional selected-center chart alone does not establish causality, network-wide representativeness, or grounds for immediate network-level advancement. Applies only to the displayed highlighted/selected high-referral screening centers and assumes the axis titles describe the plotted coordinates.",
        "evidence": "The axis labels and ticks confirm the encoding of hours (x) and referrals (y). The visual arrangement of points A through E confirms a consistent positive association (higher hours correlate with higher referrals). The condition that this applies only to the displayed centers is supported by the subtitle. The inference that this pattern is suitable for 'broader network review' but not 'immediate advancement' is supported by the fact that the data is a selected subset (selection bias) and cross-sectional (no causality), meaning it is a strong signal for investigation but not definitive proof for action.",
        "status": "supported"
      }
    }
  }
